cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use edgeofpy in your work, please cite it as below. Please also cite
  the original papers of the methods you use (listed in the function
  docstrings).
type: software
title: "edgeofpy: tools for assessing the distance to criticality in brain dynamics"
abstract: >-
  edgeofpy is a Python package for estimating the distance to criticality in
  brain dynamics, especially from M/EEG. It covers the edges of activity
  propagation (neuronal avalanches, power-law exponents, deviation from
  criticality coefficient, shape collapse, branching ratio), of synchrony
  (phase lag index, phase lag entropy, pair correlation function, global
  lability, phase-locking avalanches), of chaos (modified 0-1 chaos test,
  lambda max) and of the phases of pairwise maximum-entropy (Ising) models.
authors:
  - given-names: Jordan
    family-names: O'Byrne
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4924-4220"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jnobyrne/edgeofpy"
keywords:
  - criticality
  - neuronal avalanches
  - edge of chaos
  - synchrony
  - Ising model
  - EEG
  - MEG
  - neuroscience
